      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture of the code. Let me write an improved version of the test focusing on:\n1. Removing unused helper methods (`basic`, `isClosed`, `getReader`)\n2. Explaining the tracking format used by `trackSeen`\n3. Adding a named constant for the expected output with inline commentary\n4. Renaming the `seen` variable to something more descriptiveNow let me compile-check it.The improved test compiled successfully. The changes made were: removed four unused helper methods (`basic`, `isClosed`, `getReader`), renamed `seen` to `visitLog` for clarity, extracted the expected string into a named constant `EXPECTED_VISIT_LOG`, added a Javadoc to `trackSeen` explaining the compact format character by character, added inline comments on each `@ValueSource` input describing why it's interesting, and expanded the test-level Javadoc to explain both the regression being guarded and the expected emission order."
    }
